WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.800
New developments

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.569
swirling around embattled Congressman

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:03.536
George Santos

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.204
this morning, now

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:06.373
facing 13 federal charges.

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:08.575
The House will now not vote

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.844
on whether to kick him out of Congress.

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.145
Instead, Republicans

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:14.314
punted the issue back to the House Ethics

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:14.881
Committee, a move

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:15.882
that basically allows them

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.050
to avoid weighing in directly,

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.185
at least now on the Capitol steps.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:19.786
Last night

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:22.589
Santos vowed he is not going anywhere.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.591
And while he spoke, members

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:25.725
from the opposing parties

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.428
began to heckle Santos and each other.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.464
An investigation?

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.132
Yes, sir.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:32.899
Did you talk, Speaker

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.434
McCarthy, ahead of the vote?

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.069
No, I did not. I allowed the plot.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.838
I allowed the process to play itself out

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:42.042
the body has to kick him out.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:43.576
He's embarrassing.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:46.579
Oh, he's embarrassing Joe Biden.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:47.847
For what?

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:50.016
Oh, Biden is embarrassing.

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:50.350
Him.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.619
You got to save the party.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:54.120
Your party is hanging by.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:54.687
Got rogue.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.722
We got to get rid of Biden.

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:59.225
The party is up for these heinous crimes.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:02.829
A well-oiled

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.597
machine seen as Melina Zona

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.499
live on Capitol Hill.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:07.233
All right,

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.701
so that was quite a scene, Melanie.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.603
But what happens now?

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:12.772
Okay, so what happened yesterday

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:13.740
was House Republicans

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.041
essentially bought themselves

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.276
a little bit more time

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:16.776
when it comes

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.745
to dealing with Jorge Santos.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.080
Democrats had wanted to force

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.614
a floor vote on a resolution

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.149
that would have expelled him.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.517
But Kevin McCarthy came up

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.985
with essentially an off ramp

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.021
in order to shield his members

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.622
from having to go on the record and take

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.023
what would be

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.591
a very potentially tough vote

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.258
for some of them.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.394
So instead of voting on the resolution

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.096
itself, the House voted yesterday

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.064
to refer the resolution

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.499
to the House Ethics Committee.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.334
They voted along party lines to do that.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.235
So it now

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:43.903
heads to the House Ethics Committee.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:46.172
Essentially, this is a delay tactic.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.640
But look, the House Ethics Committee

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.542
has already been investigating

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.077
Jorge Santo since March.

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:51.644
This committee,

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:52.545
it is bipartisan,

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.280
made up of equally Republicans

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:54.981
and Democrats,

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:56.516
but it is not known to move

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.651
very quickly and in fact, John,

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.620
typically when a member is indicted,

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.555
the DOJ will ask the House Ethics

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.756
Committee to take a step back

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.492
to not interfere with their work.

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.726
However, in this case,

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.428
sources told me and my colleagues, Manu

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.662
Raju and Lauren Fox

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.797
that the House Ethics

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.999
Committee is planning to move ahead,

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.834
but that doesn't mean necessarily

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.302
that they are going to move quickly.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.370
So it could be weeks,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.239
if not months before we make them

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:20.640
see to make a recommendation

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.542
on whether or not to expel Jorge Campos.

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:23.910
And even then,

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.611
the full house

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.513
would still have to vote on expulsion,

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:28.381
which requires a two thirds majority.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.482
So all that to say,

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.283
it could be a while

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:32.118
before we see any punitive action

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.753
against Jorge Santos.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.588
But in the meantime,

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:36.589
Democrats are making clear

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:37.090
that they are not

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.424
going to let Republicans

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:39.792
live that vote down.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.594
And they are going to remind voters

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:42.962
that Jorge Santos is still,

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.631
as of right now, a current member

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.232
of the Republican Party.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:46.933
And Republicans

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:47.767
What happened, as you

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.035
so aptly point out,

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:49.903
they bought themselves

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:50.503
some time

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:51.771
where they don't have to say

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:53.072
whether they think Jorge Santos

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.375
should be in or out of Congress.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:56.709
Melania's vote to keep us posted

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.244
Thanks so much for joining the table,

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.279
Sara Matthews, former

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.380
deputy press secretary

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:00.914
for the Trump

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.815
administration, and Ashley Allison,

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.050
former national coalitions

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.752
director for the Biden-harris

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:07.053
2020 Campaign

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.154
Ladies, thank you for joining us.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:09.122
We've got Sara here

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:11.057
as well as Julia still with us.

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:13.826
I want to start with with you, Sarah.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.828
Sara Matthews.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.297
A lot of Sarah's you

00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:20.433
you heard one of the congressmen saying

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:21.734
have some dignity.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:22.902
New Yorkers need better.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.170
And this was obviously somebody

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:27.273
from New York yelling at Santos.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.642
Is he right?

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:30.910
He's 100% correct.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.579
I do wish that Jorge Santos

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:34.380
had the dignity to resign.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.014
Obviously,

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:36.616
we see that isn't going to happen.

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:37.050
He's already

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:37.884
announced his intent

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.053
to run for reelection.

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.521
But I will say

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.389
I do think it might be a little premature

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.557
to expel him

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:46.726
solely based on that indictment alone.

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:49.495
I think with, you know, in the past,

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.731
I don't recall any other member

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:52.732
or senator

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:53.866
being expelled

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.468
just based on an indictment

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:57.237
so we do need to let the Ethics

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:59.005
Committee process play out.

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:01.174
There
probably has not been another person,

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.442
though, in his position

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:03.710
that has lied so much

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:04.711
and it has been proven.

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:06.179
So I'm curious Ashleigh,

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:07.113
what you make of that

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.881
and whether you think like, hey,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.216
let's put politics aside,

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:11.551
which no one ever can, but,

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:12.452
you know, let's do this.

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:14.354
Let's look at what he has done

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.122
and say

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:18.358
this is a bad representation of us.

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:19.392
It really is.

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:20.660
I mean, as Americans,

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.362
just in general, having someone like that

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:23.730
serving in Congress,

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:24.731
I also feel really bad

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:26.032
for his constituents.

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:26.866
He says, oh,

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:28.735
they elected me to represent them.

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:30.503
No, they elected a character

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:31.871
you developed.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:34.507
They did not elect the real Jorge Santos.

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.009
Because they didn't know who he was

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.910
because he did not tell the truth.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.112
And the reality is, is

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:40.847
he isn't going to be expelled right now

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.081
because the Republicans

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:44.150
have such a slim majority in the House.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.818
Their numbers are not in their favor

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.387
when they're trying to pass legislation.

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:48.721
And so it doesn't work for them.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:49.389
And so that's

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:50.423
where the political nature

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:51.324
comes back into it.

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.859
It is not about

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.427
whether he did something wrong.

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:56.195
Everyone knows he's done something wrong,

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:58.231
but they need the votes as Republicans.

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:59.565
Right. Service.

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.601
Can I ask you a quick question on this?

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:02.735
Does it surprise you

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:03.836
where we are right now?

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:04.871
Because I feel like

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:05.772
20 years ago

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:08.107
we may not be in this position.

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:09.876
You know, it's interesting you say that.

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:11.911
I think the in the past few years,

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:13.479
especially in the digital era,

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.281
it's allowed people to create online

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.716
personalities of flat people

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:17.550
to be anonymous.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.151
It's allowed people

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:19.218
to shape their history

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:21.120
and shape their record in some senses.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:21.921
In another,

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:23.523
we have more accountability than ever

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:25.158
because you can just Google the truth.

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:26.492
And what's crazy about the Jorge

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.460
Santos story

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.294
is, by the way,

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:29.228
thank God for local news,

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.930
because there's a local Long Island paper

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:31.831
that broke the story.

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:32.965
But what's crazy about it

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:33.766
is that he was able

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:36.069
to develop this crazy persona,

00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:37.870
but also he was able

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.372
to get away with it for so long.

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:41.474
And so am I surprised that we're here?

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:42.875
In a sense, yes.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.644
Because we should have been more holding

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:46.045
our local politicians

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.613
to much more higher standards.

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:48.881
We should have been investigating them.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:50.583
We should have known this earlier.

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:51.317
But in a way, no,

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:53.186
because in the digital era, it's

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:54.620
not shocking to see people

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.789
become caricatures of themselves online.

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:58.024
And that's where we ended up

00:05:58.024 --> 00:05:58.624
where we are.

00:05:58.624 --> 00:05:59.425
And we should state

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:01.327
that the Republicans in his district

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:03.930
have called for him to step down.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.798
That has not obviously happened.

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:07.967
And that's politics.

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.235
It's also a precedent as well.

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:11.003
I think there's been two congressmen

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.372
expelled since the Civil War

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:13.473
I believe so.

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:14.807
And they were both convicted.

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:16.008
I was going to say an indictment.

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:17.343
It's not a conviction. Exactly.

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:18.644
So I guess the Republicans

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:19.979
don't do that for.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.447
And they have to clear otherwise.

